      <activity id="8e34b4ee-1b3e-58d8-80ac-51adf6d69cf6" activityNameId="a27fca93-c38e-5f53-9a5d-c38e2967e499" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, PEM, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipe [481e63394d]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, PEM, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipeline, produced by Electrolysis, SOEC with steam input using electricity from grid
This dataset represents the supply of 1 megajoule of heat in a residence, by hydrogen conversion in a fuel cell, PEM. The hydrogen is produced by  Electrolysis, SOEC with steam input, with electricity from grid as feedstock. Heat conversion efficiency [% LHV input]: 50%. LHV [MJ/kg]: 120. Market price [Euro/MJ]: 0.03. Synthesis efficiency [% LHV input]: 0%. Total cap. Input-related [kW]: 2.74. CO2 biogenic share [%]: 0%. Power [kW]: 1.6. Lifetime [years]: 4.88. Annual operation [hours]: 4100. Allocation factor: 0.12. On-site storage loss [%]: 0. Use loss [%]: 0.56. For more information, refer to: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023. Source: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: 85a7da51-a14c-3882-9338-ffbb59a0f042
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_85a7da51-a14c-3882-9338-ffbb59a0f042.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
